{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Decouple the async workflow test from the `_mcp_writes.spawn_context_daemon` import binding, or document the coupling so a spawn refactor knows to update the spy.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/interfaces/store/test_workflow_entrypoints.py:108: `from rebar import _mcp_writes`","tests/interfaces/store/test_workflow_entrypoints.py:118: `monkeypatch.setattr(_mcp_writes, \"spawn_context_daemon\", spy)`","tests/interfaces/store/test_workflow_entrypoints.py:160: `assert len(threads) == 1, threads`","src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:13: `from rebar._opcert_binding import spawn_context_daemon` (the patch only works because of this from-import binding)","src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:112: `spawn_context_daemon(_bg, name=f\"rebar-workflow-{run_id}\")`"],"finding":"The test now synchronizes by patching a private module attribute, `rebar._mcp_writes.spawn_context_daemon`. A refactor that keeps behavior the same will break it. Examples: importing the module (`from rebar import _opcert_binding`) instead of the function, moving `run_workflow`'s spawn into another helper module, or replacing the daemon with an executor. In each case the spy never fires and `assert len(threads) == 1` fails, even though `run_workflow` is still async and still reaches 'succeeded'.","id":"0","impact":0.24,"location":"tests/interfaces/store/test_workflow_entrypoints.py:105","norm_id":"n61cae3af9f149581","priority":0.2057,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":["A refactor changes `_mcp_writes` to call `_opcert_binding.spawn_context_daemon(...)` through a module import. The spy is never invoked, `threads` stays empty, and the test fails even though the MCP behavior is unchanged."],"suggested_fix":"Option 1: patch at the source, `rebar._opcert_binding.spawn_context_daemon`, and also at the `_mcp_writes` binding, so the spy survives either import style. Option 2: keep the behavior-only poll through `get_workflow_status` but use a generous deadline, e.g. loop until `time.monotonic()` passes a 120 s bound with short sleeps. That avoids both the fixed 5 s window and the internal coupling.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":false,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":true,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}}],"blocking":[],"change_fingerprint":"cf15ae36605385ad","change_id":"Idc01a43827128ff74984bf24bbfb2df224bcaf1d","coaching":[{"coaching":"Extract the duplicated logic in the thread-capture seam in the async workflow test into a shared